  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $r=13\\,\\text{in}$ and $h=19\\,\\text{in}$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\nV=\\pi (13)^{2}(19)=3\\,211\\pi {\\text{ in}}^{3}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
